<title>GERMANY: AI(R) delivers 6th ATR72 to Bangkok Airways.</title>
<headline>AI(R) delivers 6th ATR72 to Bangkok Airways.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-12-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>European aircraft manufacturer Aero International (Regional) said on Wednesday it had delivered a sixth turboprop ATR72-000 to Bangkok Airways.</p>
<p>The private Thai airline plans to operate the aircraft on its domestic flights between the Thai capital and the holiday resort of Koh Samui, an AI(R) statement released here said.</p>
<p>Bangkok Airways is also considering ordering ATR42-300 aircraft as part of expansion plans, the statement added.</p>
<p>The airline has recently opened its own airport in Sukhothai, central Thailand, in order to add new flights to Chiang Mai and northern Thailand.</p>
<p>AI(R) said it has now delivered 56 ATR aircraft to Asian-Pacific airlines and some 290 AI(R) turboprop and jet aircraft now operate in the region.</p>
<p>Aero International (Regional) is responsible for sales and marketing of aircraft of its joint owners, Aerospatiale,  British Aerospace Plc and Italy's Alenia.</p>
